# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the host KV tier SHIP-CANDIDATE gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-tier-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (STOP, no card opened): build the window image from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head: the op-fusion programme's merged work (tp4/fusion-1) and the host tier (the preconverted GDN checkpoints, the tier's
# scheduler, runner and model grafts, version 2 of the qwen_kv_read extension, built and pinned on this branch). NOTHING IS BAKED as the image default: the ship candidate's owner traffic waiver (id w2-er-fx-tier-262k-2026-10-11) is
# PENDING and c2_serving_job.read_bake refuses a PENDING profile as an image default; this image is for gate arms and smokes, never deployed. A tier arm needs the raw block ops in the image: the gate probes
# them before any container boots (c2_prefix_gate.tier_image_problems) and refuses an image without them. No privileged builder container may be up and no card job may run during the build.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line (check (g): the extension at its pin; the fusion levers' files in the overlay manifest), the Dockerfile's '[KVREAD] qwen_kv_read 2 ...' line,
# the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Duration (estimate; the last ship build measured 35 minutes): 60 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
